{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "what": "G1's frozen bounds: the anchored gap error (AGE, logits) of d1-2b-f16 through the upstream oracle against the HF reference, per settings id. compare.py gate fails on any question above them, and on observations from another computation than the identities below.",
  "rule": {
    "name": "clipped headroom",
    "cap": "0.020",
    "headroom_factor": "3",
    "floor": "0.005",
    "quantum": "0.001",
    "bound": "min(cap, max(floor, ceil(headroom_factor * M, quantum))), M the representative set's max AGE",
    "preconditions": "M <= cap / 2, and every changed discrete answer consistent with the bound",
    "predeclared": "P11 acceptance plan v2, item b, before any F16 oracle observation existed"
  },
  "rationale": [
    "The cap, 0.020 logits for both settings, is a predeclared quality requirement under test, not an established noise bound: no F16 Flash Attention data existed when it was set. Flash Attention gets no allowance of its own; a failure of cpu-t4-fa-on blocks the product default.",
    "The bound is absolute and covers every offered group: the error of a gap is the hidden state's error projected on the difference of two label rows of the LM head, which does not scale with the gap.",
    "The headroom factor and the floor are engineering margins, not statistical guarantees; the clipped rule guarantees at least twice the representative maximum (recorded as headroom.ratio).",
    "If a set exceeds its bound the gate fails and the cause is investigated; the bound is never widened to make it pass. A changed target or default is a new experiment."
  ],
